    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0868" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3273: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Culbertson</hi>)<anchor n="4" xml:id="d553-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-05T11:00:00-05:00">March 5, 1929—11
                    a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>20. Your 27, March 3, noon. I expect to remain as Secretary of State until about
                    March 25 at which time my successor, Mr. Henry L. Stimson, will arrive. I wish
                    to do everything in my power during this time to further a complete
                    settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d553-f1" n="4" type="source" xml:id="d553-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date to the
                    Ambassador in Peru as telegram No. 19.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
